{
  "name": "Sticker intake and sheet generation",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Sticker intake and sheet generation\\n\\nImported from sticker/n8n/ in the nix-config repo. This file was generated without access to an n8n instance: after importing, open each node and confirm its settings, then run a test submission with disposable art.\\n\\nAll processing is done by the `sticker-tool` command. Customer text is never placed in a command line.\\n\\nSet this workflow's Error Workflow (Settings) to 'Sticker error notify'.\\n\\n'Product' and 'Existing listing' are plain text fields, not dropdowns -- this n8n's Form/Wait node could not set a dropdown's option list from an expression (confirmed: the expression only ever reached Default Value, never Field Options -> Values). Leave either field blank to mean \"new\": blank Product + filled New product letters starts a brand-new product; blank Existing listing starts the next new listing under an already-known product. Typed values are re-validated against the real list in a Code node before anything reaches a command line.\\n\\n'Product' is deliberately read from a different place than 'Existing listing'. list-products scans the read-only design-asset library (Shop-Assets, by folder name only -- it is the business's real, pre-existing catalog) for which 3-letter codes exist at all. list-listings then scans sticker-tool's own outbox for what has actually been produced under the one chosen prefix -- most prefixes will show no existing listings yet, since the asset library predates this tool.\\n\\nThe approval form's Sheet previews field uses an html field type to embed the preview JPGs as base64 -- unverified against a live n8n, confirm it actually renders images rather than raw HTML text.\\n\\nHand-adjusting a layout: open the exported <SKU>_<sheet>.svg from staging in Inkscape, move pieces (no rotate/scale/skew), then run `sticker-tool apply-svg-layout --job <id> --sku <SKU> --sheet <type>` by hand. That command is not wired into the approval dropdown yet -- it is a manual follow-up step, not part of this workflow.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "067519ea-7e95-5f6c-8403-e43faed98f17",
      "name": "Read me",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "formTitle": "New sticker listing",
        "formDescription": "Upload the artwork for ONE new listing. Each file becomes one variation (V001, V002, ...) of the next listing number.",
